From a18ea0af03eed0957783a2255179d80093ed7ec6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:43:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] STORE S6: ATAPI + El Torito -- any ISO boots like VirtualBox

--cdrom= attaches an ATAPI CD to HBA ctrl 0 port 1 (conflicts with
--sata-port1=).  The port reports PxSIG 0xEB14 and answers 0xA1
IDENTIFY PACKET DEVICE with word0 0x8580 (removable CD-ROM), so stock
SeaBIOS classifies the drive as "DVD/CD [AHCI/1: ... ATAPI-0 DVD/CD]";
ATA disks keep aborting 0xA1 so SeaBIOS falls back to IDENTIFY DEVICE
(pinned as an NC).

0xA0 PACKET executes the SCSI CDB at ct+0x40 (byte count in the FIS
lba_mid/lba_high pair): 0x00 TUR, 0x03 REQUEST SENSE (18 B, autosense
consumed on read), 0x12 INQUIRY (36 B, type 5 + removable + AURALITE /
EmuCD), 0x1A MODE SENSE(6) (write-protect + geometry page), 0x1B START
STOP, 0x1E PREVENT, 0x25 READ CAPACITY (2048-byte blocks), 0x28
READ(10) (2048-B sectors through ahci_dma_xfer with byte-granular
image offsets), 0x43 READ TOC (one track, LBA 0).  Unknown CDBs take
CHECK CONDITION (sense 5/20, PxIS.TFES + TFD.ERR + ABRT), WRITE(10)
reports sense 7/27 (data protect); any later success clears autosense.
test_engine_atapi pins the whole surface incl. the sense lifecycle and
the two negative controls.

Machine shape and snapshots carry the new state: sata_kind[][] joins
the shape check (a CD snapshot cannot load against a disk setup) and
the port sense fields ride the existing ahci_snap.  Lane C of
tests/test_iso_boot.py is live (it SKIP-gated on usage: until now):
stock SeaBIOS boots the 1 MiB El Torito test ISO from --cdrom= and
prints the stub marker (measured 7.9 s wall).  The GUI wizard's "select
an ISO" now uses this path (normal_config iso -> --cdrom=), and expert
mode exposes the option through the SCHEMA.  docs/WINDOWS.md section E
carries the note that the desktop GUI automates the manual recipe.

Measured flake fixed in the launcher WS test: the monitor's state push
coalesces into the same TCP segment as the 101 response about one run
in six, and the test's header-only reader discarded that tail (2/12
standalone failures), then parsed mid-frame garbage through the whole
lifecycle block.  The test keeps the prefix in a WSock reader like
production MonitorClient already did; 15/15 clean re-runs after.

Gates (sequential): make test rc=0 (589 ok; both ISO lanes live: Q
8.3 s disk route, C 7.9 s ATAPI route), make test-sanitize rc=0
(267 ok), make fuzz (512 programs / 12288 states match).
